summary: Duplicates: list the groups of byte-identical files, or scan for them

!! Reference

```
Duplicates: list the groups of byte-identical files, or scan for them

The scan writes its conclusion — one `duplicate_group` metarecord per set, referenced by its members through `mfr_duplicate_group` — so the listing is an ordinary query and "what else is identical to this file" is `same(mfr_duplicate_group, <uuid>)`. `keep` and `trash` send copies to the trash by a query, never a group's last one.

Usage: mf duplicate [COMMAND]

Commands:
  list   List the duplicate groups, worst reclaimable space first — the default
  scan   Scan for byte-identical files and record the groups
  keep   Keep the copies a query matches: trash their twins outside it
  trash  Trash the copies a query matches, where a twin exists outside it
  clear  Delete every duplicate group and every link to one (the hashes are kept)
  help   Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
```
